Problem: Users have no visibility into token consumption across sessions or individual checkpoints, making it difficult to diagnose unexpected costs, identify inefficient workflows, or compare token usage between different approaches.
Solution: Added two diagnostic commands that surface token data from session metadata. entire session tokens shows per-session breakdowns with input/output/cache metrics, filtering by session ID, time range, or agent type. entire checkpoint tokens <id> displays token usage for a single checkpoint and compares it against the branch average, highlighting anomalies and recommending optimizations (like switching models or enabling prompt caching). Both commands render visual bars, agent-specific terminology, and actionable guidance to help users reduce costs.

